-- reader-first.l4's RAND, evaluated twice: once by #EVAL and once by
-- #EVALTRACE, which also prints how it was evaluated. The sides of a RAND
-- take the trace's events in step either way, so `possession`'s read at 400
-- sees the notice recorded at 10 and both give the same answer. Before
-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1069 both gave an answer that missed the notice; on the
-- first build of the fix the traced one stopped with an error instead.

DECLARE Party IS ONE OF Landlord
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF `gives notice`, `seeks possession`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`notice` MEANS
    PARTY Landlord
    MAY `gives notice`
    WITHIN 100
    HENCE COMMIT `notice given` IS TRUE HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`possession` MEANS
    PARTY Landlord
    MAY `seeks possession` PROVIDED (RECALL OFFICIAL's `notice given`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    WITHIN 1000
    HENCE COMMIT `possession sought` IS TRUE HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the tenancy` MEANS `possession` RAND `notice`

#EVAL EVALTRACE `the tenancy` 0 (LIST EVENT Landlord `gives notice` 10, EVENT Landlord `seeks possession` 400)
#EVALTRACE EVALTRACE `the tenancy` 0 (LIST EVENT Landlord `gives notice` 10, EVENT Landlord `seeks possession` 400)
